<title>UK: Baltic/Black Sea exports fell to 1.75 mpbd last weEK.</title>
<headline>Baltic/Black Sea exports fell to 1.75 mpbd last weEK.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of crude oil and refined products from Baltic and Black Sea terminals slipped 110,000 barrels a day (bpd) to 1.75 million bpd in the third week of April from 1.86 million the week before, consultancy Petro Logistics said.</p>
<p>The total was down 220,000 bpd from 1.97 million bpd in the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports rose by 108,000 bpd on the week to 1.04 million bpd. This was 164,000 bpd down on year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports were 270,300 bpd, down 37,000 bpd on the week and up 64,000 bpd on the year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports at 401,000 bpd were 68,000 bpd down week-on-week and 92,000 bpd down year-on-year.</p>
